"<strong>Q4.</strong> Sodium's two lines are {#} nm and {#} nm. How far does the mirror move between fadings of the rings, and why do they not disappear completely?",
"<strong>Q5.</strong> As M₁ moves to make the arms more unequal, do rings come out of the center or sink into it? Why are there more rings across the screen when the arms are very unequal?",
"<strong>\"Moving the mirror by λ moves one fringe.\"</strong> The light goes there and back: one fringe for every λ/{#} of mirror travel.",
"<strong>\"The gas changes the wavelength of the laser.\"</strong> It changes the wavelength inside the gas, λ/n, so the cell holds more wavelengths; the laser's own wavelength is unchanged.",
"<strong>\"Equal paths can be found with the laser.\"</strong> A laser's fringes look the same at any setting (only the ring size changes); white light finds equal paths.",
